From ed1d64d9a3016abc83cad6656bec808c5280f884 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 19:58:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08378/11362] REQ-ARC-WMTE-6180: generic budget-meter
 exhaustion estimate (default-off, unwired)

A per-level action/click budget meter (exhaust it -> GAME_OVER) was
independently hand-documented in 6+ games (r11l, sc25, s5i5, g50t,
bp35) with no shared code. region_hud_evidence already recognizes
this region shape generically; this adds a scalar 'actions remaining
until exhaustion' estimate on top of an admitted region, plus a pure
additive search-cost consumer -- no per-game constants, no source
reading, no oracle.

Adversarial review caught two real bugs before this ever shipped
wired to anything: (1) a whole-trajectory OLS fit is structurally
biased positive after any early jump, silently masking the test's
own key assertion behind a guard that never fired; (2) no per-level-
reset awareness, an 8x overestimate in the unsafe direction on the
exact mainline case (every named game resets its meter on level-up).
Fixed both: segment-aware (mirrors region_hud_evidence's own restart
rule) + a sliding recent-transitions window instead of a whole-
segment fit. Both findings are now regression tests.

Ships default-off (BUDGET_AWARE_SEARCH_ENABLED=False) and NOT wired
into E3AgentPolicy/plan_in_model -- wiring is separate, empirically-
validated follow-up work per the Phase Prototype discipline.
